\end{equation*}
Here, $U$ is a random unitary drawn from a unitary $k$-design with $\epsilon/2$ additive error, it acts on a subsystem $M$ of $N_M$ qubits, and $V$ is a global Clifford unitary drawn from an exact Clifford $k$-design. The ensemble $\calE$ can realize a unitary $k$-design with $\epsilon$ additive error for $N_M = O(k^3+\log(1/\epsilon))$
