\begin{rem}\label{hns}
Finally, for $d\ge 4$,  we remark that  the $\epsilon$-loss in \eqref{smooth-pq0} can be removed in a certain range of $p,q$, which is even broader  than the range in Theorem \ref{improved}.  The optimal local smoothing estimate \eqref{localsmoothing0} without the loss $N^{\epsilon}$  was  obtained by 
