\subsubsection{Controlled sampling dynamics for fa7 and jak2 proteins}
%
We illustrate the controlled sampling dynamics on the diffusion manifold $\mathcal{M}_T$ for fa7 in Figure \ref{fig:fa7_reward} and jak2 in Figure \ref{fig:jak2_reward}. We observe that SDG without the Stein correction overestimates the true (genuine) rewards, yielding artificially high reward values. However, the generated molecules are often unrealistic, exhibiting low QED and SA scores. More critically, this reward overestimation can mislead the score models into a false convergence, as shown for jak2 in Figure \ref{fig:jak2_reward}.d, where the falsely high rewards incorrectly infer that no further improvement is necessary, resulting in flattened gradients. In contrast, SDG introduces a low-cost Stein-based regularization to mitigate reward overestimation. In addition, SDG-regularized models evolve smoothly over the sampling steps, ensuring that sampling remains within generative manifolds, particularly in low-density sampling regimes. 

