\section{Constraint on the deformation parameter of Sgr A*} \label{sec:constraint}
%-----------------------------------------------------------------%
In this section, we aim to give a constraint on the deformation parameter $\gamma$ of Sgr A* by using the obtained PN expansion formula~\eqref{ZV_peri_PN}. The periapsis shift of S2 has been observed by the Gravity Collaboration~\cite{GRAVITY:2020gka} as
\begin{align}
    \Delta \phi_\text{S2} = f_\text{SP} \frac{6 \pi M}{p}, \quad f_\text{SP} = 1.1 \pm 0.19, \label{eq_peri_S2}
\end{align}
where $f_\text{SP}$ is the non-dimensional factor which denotes the deviation from the 1PN order term of the PN expansion formula for the periapsis shift in the Schwarzschild spacetime (see Eq.~\eqref{eq:PN_S}). Assuming that the deviation $f_\text{SP}$ is a contribution from the 2PN order of the PN expansion formula in the ZV spacetime, we can rewrite Eq.~\eqref{eq_peri_S2} as
\begin{align}
    \frac{6 \pi M}{p} + \left[ \left(44+\frac{12}{\gamma}-\frac{2}{\gamma ^2}\right)+3\left(-3+\frac{4}{\gamma }\right) e^2 \right] \frac{\pi M^2}{2 p^2} = f_\text{SP} \frac{6 \pi M}{p}.
\end{align}
Solving this equation for $f_\text{SP}$, we obtain
\begin{align}
    f_\text{SP} = 1 + \left[ \left(44+\frac{12}{\gamma}-\frac{2}{\gamma ^2}\right) - 3 \left(3-\frac{4}{\gamma }\right) e^2 \right] \frac{M}{12 p}. \label{func_f_gamma}
\end{align}
It can be found that $f_\text{SP}$ is the quadratic function of $1/\gamma$ and has a maximum value 
\begin{align}
    f_\text{SP,max} = 1 + \left( 31 + \frac{27}{2} e^2 + 9 e^4 \right) \frac{M}{6p}, \label{f_max}
\end{align}
at $\gamma = 1/[3(1+e^2)]$ or $\tilde{M}_2 = 8/3 + 6 e^2 + 3 e^4 $.

We plot Eq.~\eqref{func_f_gamma} for the S2-Sgr A* system in Fig.~\ref{fig:plot_f}. Fig.~\ref{fig:plot_f_overall} shows an overall plot of $f_\text{SP}$. The region $f_\text{SP}<0.91$, which is restricted by the observation, is filled in grey. Fig.~\ref{fig:plot_f_nmv} shows an enlarged plot of Fig.~\ref{fig:plot_f_overall} near the maximum value, and Fig.~\ref{fig:plot_f_gamma} is the plot with $1/\gamma$ as the horizontal axis. Table~\ref{table:paras_consts} in Appendix~\ref{app:paras} presents the orbital parameters of S2-Sgr A* and some constants we have used to plot. 

