Physically, this confirms the expected periodic alternation of concentrated curvature around defect positions in the grain boundary, and highlights the singular nature of the geometric response in the conformal metric. The logarithmic plot thus provides a clear visualization of the curvature landscape, especially in regimes where standard linear plots fail to resolve spatial features with high gradients.
