\abstract{The Muon g-2 experiment at Fermilab seeks to measure the muon magnetic moment anomaly, $a_\mu =(g-2)/2$, with a final target precision of 0.14 parts-per-million (ppm). The experiment’s initial result,
published in 2021 using Run 1 data from 2018, confirmed the previous measurement at Brookhaven
