We conduct $N$-body simulations using {\sc Rebound} and its extension package, {\sc Reboundx} \citep{rebound,reboundx}, considering an HR 8799-like system consisting of a central star with mass $1.52\ M_\odot$, the four observed planets with masses from the inside out \rev{(}$\{8.0,9.5,7.5,6.0\}$ $M_{\rm jup}$\rev{)} and an outer debris disc composed of massless particles. The case with a potential fifth planet is presented in Section \ref{sec:five-planets scenario}.
