\begin{abstract}
In this paper, we define a new concept of Noetherian commutative rings which stands between
\gor\ and \cm\ properties.
We show that this new property keep hold under common operations of commutative rings
such as localization, polynomial extension and under mild assumptions, flat extension, tensor product,
Segre product and so on.
We show that for Schubert cycles, the Ehrhart rings of cycle graphs and perfect graphs, this new
concept is close to \gor\ property.
\\
MSC: 13H10, 14M15, 05E40, 05C25, 52B20\\
%52B20, 05E40, 05C17, 05C38\\
 {\bf Keywords}: \gor, \cm, trace ideal, canonical module
\end{abstract}


