\section{Discussion}

\subsection{AGN contribution} \label{subsec:agn_contribution}

%log10[SFR] = 0.75 × log10[L1.4] − 15.96
% 1e+38 at 6*(1+0.3)=7.8 GHz (rest-frame), Lnu = 1.28e+28 erg/s/Hz
% Lnu at 1.4 GHz = (7.8/1.4)^{0.8} * 1.28e+28 = 5.06e+28 erg/s/Hz = 5.06e+21 W/Hz
% lgSFR = 0.318; SFR = 2.1

We discuss the possibility that the radio emission of AT2020ysg and AT2020qhs is powered by pre-existing active galactic nuclei (AGN)\footnote{To produce a radio luminosity of $\gtrsim 10^{38}\,{\rm erg\,s^{-1}}$ via star formation, the required star formation rate would be $\gtrsim 2.1\,M_\odot\,{\rm yr^{-1}}$, which is not consistent with host galaxy population synthesis analysis. Therefore, star formation is unlikely to be the source of the radio emission.}. 
