At high pressures, our calculations align closely with experimental data~\cite{wolanin1997equation,sugimura2008compression,asahara2010thermoelastic}. 
Below $60~\text{GPa}$, values from different experiments exhibit a spread of approximately $2$ to $5~\text{GPa}$ at each volume, and the NCT results fall within this range.

